Z||000005||DKOV||10-11-2001||01:13 AM||||I am in proress myself...  Also with NO instructions.  Seems pretty common in this industry, especially where the 355 is concerned.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>What is the kit manufacturer that you are working on?  That will tell alot about the "hows" when building your kit...<P>Of course, in reality, there are only a couple of 355 kits that ARE different.  Most 355 body kits are a dupe of a dupe of a dupe.<P>Eagle, IFG/Warlock, Perry and God only knows how many others are simply copies of each other.  Depending on which kit you bought, you may have a fifth generation copy.<P>The only other kit that is truly unique is the Mirage kit.  To my knowledge, they built their own and nobody has duped it to this day.<P>I searched high and low before buying my kit and I ended up getting a Mirage.  I also purchased a IFG/Warlock kit from a former IFG employee who took my money and never delivered the body!  $5000.00 down, let's try again...<P>Although I am not happing about loosing my money and sending an attorney after the bastage, I believe there was a silver liner... The Mirage 355.  I was able to find and purchase this stellar kit and am SOOOO very glad I did.  Hands down, a much better kit.<P>Just take the fact that the Mirage is a 21 piece kit versus the usual 9 pieces that the IFG style kit provides.  The Mirage is perfect right down to the panels!<P>Anyway, So far, I have spared no expense in preparation of this conversion.  I have purchased a full set of lights, lenses, badges, wheel discs and steel work from a Ferrari Dealership and, in addition, a full complete authentic 355 Interior with venting and badges.  The shifter is authentic 355 modified to fit the fiero setup as a short shift.  I also aquired some Ferrari emmissions and door sill aluminum decals to place inside the door well upon completion.<P>The "Donor" is an 88 Fiero GT with race history.  It has been upgraded to a 3.4L Dual Twin Cam with ported and polished upper and lower intake manifolds, tuned heads, minor valve work, Fuel Pressure regulator, underdrive pulley, custom exhaust, etc.  The motor is putting aut around 300 HP although I have yet to have it dynoed.  I'll be doing that in the next few weeks.  It pulls HARD and will break the tires loose all the way into 3rd... well, before I put the AVS Sports on there  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  I'm hoping to have the car into the high 12s or low 13s eventually.<P>The chassis has been dropped 1.5 inches and currently sports a full race-Poly bushing set, Koni adjustable coil-overs, 300# Eibach springs, 17inch Koenig Rayne rims wrapped in Yokohama AVS Sprot tires, a MASSIVE 13 (yes 13) inch brakes!  A complete Wilwood Brake system with Zinc plated Gold rotors with four piston Billet Calipers powder coated red, Wilwood e-brake calipers, race/sport "T" compound Wilwood pads, steel braded brake hoses.<P>Additional items for the conversion not installed yet include a Held Motorsport WIDE track slalom conversion built to fit the new body (plus 8 inched in the rear and plus 4 inches in the front) so I won't need or use wheel spacers.  The widetrack system also provides complete adjustability for Camber and Castor angles too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I have done SOME work on the body itself, isolated to the front and rear bumpers.  I needed to modify them to fit the authentic Ferrari light buckets and lenses.  The stock "holes" were not large enough.  I've also begun work on the front Grill.<P>I've been waiting for the rains to come to pull the Fiero into the Garage to begin its transformation.  Guess what?  It's RAINING!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I am keeping a "build diary" and taking lots of pics.  Currently, the majority of the pics show the engine work and chassis work progressing.  Pretty boring unless you are into the "guts" of the Ferrari.  I also have pics of the body kit all laid out with lenses, badges etc.<P>Ove the winter, I will be taking some pics of the build so I'll be sure to post them to my Photopoint Account for you all to see  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>ADRIFT... let's definately keep in touch.  I'm sure that we can help each other out from time to time!  E-mail me if you like!<P>Good Luck!<P>DKOV -||||reg||1
