Z||000008||Spyder||10-11-2001||06:16 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.markalexandermiller.com/1aredc.JPG"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.markalexandermiller.com/1aredd.JPG"> <BR>I picked her up Tuesday from the paint shop.<BR>She looks better than I expected, and the pics do not do the car justice.<BR>Building this car has taken a lot of Time….. Money….. Blood…..Strain on relationship…...Sweat…... Worry….. Frustration…... other than all that, the experience has been great. lol  If I ever do it again, I will not go all out like on this one. <BR>I’ll post more pics when I can.<P>Adrift, you would not believe the attention this thing gets just sitting on a trailer  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>It makes you feel like a five year old on Christmas day.<BR>||||reg||12
Z||000009||Spektrum-87GT||10-11-2001||07:33 PM||||dkov: was the mirage made by euroworks? they make a lambo kit now thats called 'mirage', i know that ferrari cracked down on kit makers, so they probably switched over to lamborghini. Lamborghini rules! they have yet to push the issue, maybe its because they realize not everyone can afford a real one! or the maintainence!||||reg||1
Z||000010||DKOV||10-11-2001||10:17 PM||||Spektrum...<P>No.  Euroworks makes the Countach kit CALLED a Mirage.  In my case, the 355 kit was from a MANUFACTURER called Mirage.  Product name versus a company name...  I can understand the confusion  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Mirage (the company) was indeed "visited" by Ferrari and have since gone WAAAAY out of business  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  If you are lucky, you might find one of these amazing kits around, but expect to pay around $10,000 for the BODY KIT alone!<P>By the way, Spyder's 355 project looks TERRIFIC!!!  Where did you get it painted and how much?<P>DKOV -||||reg||1
Z||000011||MinnGreenGT||10-12-2001||09:46 AM||||Earlier this year I did a lot of research on the F355 kits... and yes, the Mirage is absolutely the best thing out there.  Check out this website for some build/finished pics of a Mirage (which has since been sold I belive) <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Pit/6426/myF355.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Pit/6426/myF355.html</A> <P>I actually took a trip from Minnesota to South Carolina to look at a partially completed F355 Berlinetta (I don't like the spyder as well- that's just be though). I asked the seller numerous times if he knew who the manufacturer was, but he insisted that he never knew.  I got down there to find a JLGi (Jay Lucas Group Int'l) instruction manual! DAMNIT! If I'd know it was a JLGI, I'd never have even made the trip.<P>One thing to look for for authenticity (not that most people would notice) is the lower rocker panel.  On a real F355 it is one piece, on many Replicas, it is split and opens with the door.  Just an observation- not a criticism (I love spyder's Spyder in the pics BTW).||||reg||1
Z||000012||DKOV||10-12-2001||10:19 AM||||MinnGreenGT...<P>Ironically, that page you posted... the reference to "another kit"...  That is the guy I bought it from!!!  I've seen that actual car and now am the proud owner of the kit!  As you can see... TOTALLY authentic!<P>That is what is so great about the Mirage 355!!!<P>Every panel on the car is AS THE ORIGINAL.  I've often been a major critic of the "one piece" panels on most 355 kits out there.  The JGLI is a copy of the Perry which is a copy of the IFG, so naturally, they all have the very same singular design that makes them look... well... bad.<P>Don't get me wrong, they are still a beautiful car, just don't get to close and NEVER EVER show one with the doors OPEN.<P>Also, those body kits do not have rocker panels as does the original.  The front end is a "clip" with the fenders, bumper and trim parts all being of ONE piece.  The rear clip is the same way.  Rear fenders, rear bumper, upper tail panel and the tail light panel itself should all be separate.<P>The Mirage 355 is just exacltly that.  the front end, for instance... instead of being one clip with two light pods and a lid, it is two separate fenders, front bumper, front facia trim, two head lamps and a two pience deck lid (inner & outer).  The rear end receives a similar treatment with all separated panels.<P>As mentioned above, the DOORS are the biggest giveaway though.  Especially when they are open!  A Real 355 has a rocker panel that incorporates a smaller scoop of the same design as the larger door scoop.  This smaller scoop/rocker panels should STAY IN PLACE when the door is opened!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The mirage 355 does.<P>Another nice detail is the structure of the front decklid.  It is more accurate and does not include that nasty notch that the IFG, etc. does...<P>If you can find one, GRAB IT!!!  The Mirage is WORTH EVERY PENNY!!!<P>I know I ramble, but this car is terrific   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>DKOV -<p>[This message has been edited by DKOV (edited 10-12-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000013||MinnGreenGT||10-12-2001||12:05 PM||||DKOV-- DAMNYOU!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I really wanted Tony's mirage kit.  You are so lucky!<P>The JLGi was the biggest piece of crap piece of fiberglass I've ever seen. I'd have had to spend at least $10-15K just to get the body lines straight.  Avoid at all costs (unless you are a wiz with Fiberglass).||||reg||1
Z||000014||mshill||10-12-2001||01:18 PM||||I am not building an F355, but an knee deep in an F50 project.  I just love the lines of the F50.  I am also working from virtually no instructions.  I received a single sheet of paper with a few hand drawings and some really poor hand written notes like "tilt radiator down 3 inches".  Judging by the little instruction I have received, I am glad that I am building it myself instead of getting a turnkey.  I have had the kit since January and am just now starting to get into some of the final fitting of the rocker panels and the front cowling (one piece hood).  I have to admit, however, that the fiberglass quality is top notch especially compared to some of the stuff that I have seen others struggling with on the net.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000015||MinnGreenGT||10-12-2001||01:21 PM||||mshill- who/where did you get the kit from?||||reg||1
Z||000016||Spyder||10-13-2001||02:25 AM||||<BR>Prtzlboy: lol  clearest windshield  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I really liked the mirage.  I tried to get one of them mirages, but them suckers were gone.  If I remember right the only thing I didn’t like was it was the short wheel base.<P>If you know Ferraris, you’ll know mine is fake, my interior is so different from the real deal.<BR>Oh Yeah, check out my Mercedes Benz mirror lights, I love them lights.<P>DKOV<BR>I had the car painted in Florida, $2,500 painted which included the body prep (bondoing) and primer.<P>Here is a pic of the interior so far. I lightened up the pic for better viewing.  The door panels are on top of that TV.<P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.markalexandermiller.com/1arede.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||DKOV||10-13-2001||04:29 AM||||Spyder...<P>Interior looks great.  I wouldn't worry about it looking REAL as long as it doesn't look like a Fiero.  Not that there's anything WRONG with a Fiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The one thing that I have always been disappointed with on a REAL 355 is the interior!  My Lotus Esprit Turbo is the same way... square, flat, unispired.  You'd think that either of these exotics would put just a LITTLE time into creature comforts.<P>Of course, that is now why you buy a Super Car now is it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I'll see if I can't start scanning in all these pics so I can show you my progress as well.  I only wish I was as far along with my project as you are, Mr "I just got it back from the paint shop"   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>So, how in the world did you get it done for only $2500!??!?  Did you do the prep work yourself?  What a steal.  I've not been able to get any lower than $5000 - $7500 for the job!  Good show!<P>Keep me informed on your progress...  I love following the "process".<P>PS... Like the mirrors  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>DKOV -||||reg||1
Z||000018||DKOV||10-13-2001||04:31 AM||||MSHill...<P>Got pics ?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>DKOV -||||reg||1
Z||000019||rogergarrison||10-13-2001||02:26 PM||||all the pics look great. Euro works makes 2 Lambos, 1 for stock wb, 1 for lengthened one. There are tons of 355 body kits on ebay. just search 'Ferrari' and 'Kitcars/Repicas'<P>I come close to buying 2 kits last week. one was a 355 Spyder and one was a Berlinetta, both kits  for $3,700 in Florida. The dealers for them just moved onto Ebay to sell them as 'owners' not as a business. That way Ferrari cant do a thing to them unless everyone lets the secret out  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Youll see what I mean when you notice a lot of similar kits are all from same seller, or in some cases just use a diff ID.<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=11878523&p=52990885"> ||||reg||1
Z||000020||Spyder||10-14-2001||10:56 PM||||The paint job was a deal, I built a website for the guy for free, so he gave me a good deal on the paint job. <BR>But since I just paid him for the paint job I’m now broke again.  I work, save money for a car part. Buy the car part and then repeat the process. Thank goodness there is a lot of stuff that I can do now that just requires my time to do. Does anyone know where I can pick up some “spare time”?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I'll post some more as I make progress.<BR>Make sure you guys post your progress pics.||||reg||1
