Z||000022||artherd||10-15-2001||04:59 AM||||Sigh.... I came *this* close to doing a 355 myself. <P>Then I drove the real thing.<P>I am now *totally* hooked, and am going to keep my Fieros as fieros (ok, so I'm making them into as much a Ferrari as they can be, down to a 4-cam 4.6litre v8  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>But oh my GOD, that 'cinqu'ivalve Ferrari ENGINE!!!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000023||mshill||10-15-2001||10:46 AM||||DKOV, MinnGreenGT,<P>I don't have a digital camera yet.  I will take some pictures for a build diary and get them on CD though.  See <A HREF="http://www.bodykitz.com" TARGET=_blank>www.bodykitz.com</A>  for the pictures of the F50-like-kit.  The manufacturer of the body panels is kind of hiding from the Ferrari people as well.  Looks like there is only one more F50-like set of panels available.   From my understanding they won't be making any more Ferrari look-alikes at all.  Too much of a hassle for them legally.  <BR>||||reg||1
